  Layer       : 1
  Category    : SQL Optimization → Join Optimization
  Similarity  : 0.4722
  Title       : Use broadcast join for small lookup table joins
  Problem     : Joining a large fact table with a small lookup or dimension table using a default shuffle join causes unnecessary cross-network data movement, increasing execution time and resource consumption.
  Strategy    : Use a broadcast join hint to replicate the small table to all executors, eliminating the shuffle phase entirely.
  Conditions  : []
---
